parts":[{"text":"வள்","lemma":"வள்","gloss":"thick"}],"gloss":"thick"},{"surface":"இதழ்","parts":[{"text":"இதழ்","lemma":"இதழ்","gloss":"petal"}],"gloss":"petals"},{"surface":"அவிழ்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"அவிழ்","lemma":"அவிழ்","gloss":"blossom"},{"text":"ந்த","lemma":"ந்த","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"blossomed"},{"surface":"தாமரை","parts":[{"text":"தாமரை","lemma":"தாமரை","gloss":"lotus"}],"gloss":"lotus"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நள்","parts":[{"text":"நள்","lemma":"நள்","gloss":"deep"}],"gloss":"deep"},{"surface":"இரும்","parts":[{"text":"இரும்","lemma":"இரும்","gloss":"vast"}],"gloss":"vast"},{"surface":"பொய்கையும்","parts":[{"text":"பொய்கை","lemma":"பொய்கை","gloss":"pond"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the pond"},{"surface":"தீயும்","parts":[{"text":"தீ","lemma":"தீ","gloss":"fire"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"and the fire"},{"surface":"ஓர்","parts":[{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஓர்","gloss":"one/same"}],"gloss":"same"},{"surface":"அற்றே","parts":[{"text":"அற்று","lemma":"அற்று","gloss":"nature"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"are of the same nature"}]}],"literal":"Many wise men! Many wise men! / without saying \"go\", preventing [me] saying \"stay back\", / of evil counsel, many wise men! / Sliced with a sword, the striped curved cucumber, cooked / like its seeds, without touching the good, pale, fragrant ghee, / squeezed by hand, lying between leaves, the ball of rice, / with white sesame paste and added sour tamarind, cooked / Vēḷai greens as boiled food, / on a bed strewn with gravel, without a mat, sleeping / suffering widows we are not indeed! / Prepared in the great cremation ground, with black logs, the funeral pyre, / let it be difficult for you, but for us, our / great-shouldered husband having died, completely / with thick petals blossomed, the lotus / deep, vast pond and the fire are of the same nature.","translation":"O men of great wisdom! O men of great wisdom! You who give me evil counsel, preventing me from going with my husband and telling me to stay back! We are not the kind of suffering widows who eat only boiled vēḷai greens cooked with white sesame paste and sour tamarind, squeezed by hand into a ball and served on leaves, without touching the pale, fragrant ghee that looks like the seeds of a sliced cucumber, and who sleep on a bed of gravel without a mat! Let the funeral pyre of black logs prepared in the great cremation ground be a difficult thing for you. For us, since our husband of great shoulders has died, the deep, vast pond where the thick-petalled lotus blossoms and the burning fire are exactly the same.","modern":"பல சான்றோர்களே! பல சான்றோர்களே! என்னை என் கணவனுடன் செல்லுமாறு கூறாமல், 'இங்கே தங்கிவிடு' என்று தடுத்து நிறுத்தும் தீய அறிவுரை கூறும் சான்றோர்களே! வெட்டப்பட்ட வெள்ளரிக்காயின் விதை போன்ற, நல்ல வெண்மையான நறுமணமுள்ள நெய்யைத் தொடாமல், இலைகளுக்கு இடையே வைத்து கைகளால் பிழிந்த சோற்றுத் திரளோடு, வெள்ளை எள்ளின் விழுதும் புளியும் சேர்த்துச் சமைத்த வேளைக் கீரையை உணவாகக் கொண்டு, பருக்கைக் கற்கள் பரப்பிய படுக்கையில் பாய் இல்லாமல் படுத்துறங்கும் துன்புறும் கைம்பெண்கள் அல்லேம் நாம்! சுடுகாட்டில் கரிய விறகுகளால் அமைக்கப்பட்ட இந்த ஈமத்தீயில் இறங்குவது உங்களுக்கு அரியதாக இருக்கலாம். ஆனால், பெரிய தோள்களை உடைய எம் கணவன் மறைந்த பின்பு, இதழ்கள் விரிந்த தாமரைகள் மலர்ந்த குளிர்ந்த பொய்கையும், இந்த எரியும் தீயும் எமக்கு ஒன்றே ஆகும்.","explanation":"The speaker is Queen Peruṅkōppeṇṭu, the wife of King Pūtap Pāṇṭiyaṉ, who has decided to perform Sati on her husband's funeral pyre. The wise elders of the court try to dissuade her, advising her to live as a widow instead. She rejects their advice, calling it 'evil counsel' because she refuses to live the miserable, austere life expected of a widow. She describes this life in detail: eating tasteless boiled greens with sesame paste and no ghee, and sleeping on gravel. To her, entering the burning fire of the pyre is as cool and welcoming as a deep, vast pond filled with blooming lotuses. The key words are 'ஈமம்' (funeral pyre), 'உயவற் பெண்டிரேம்' (suffering widows), and 'பொய்கையும் தீயும் ஓரற்றே' (the pond and the fire are of the same nature).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}